<title>RUSSIA: Russia govt institute sees 96 oil output 303 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russia govt institute sees 96 oil output 303 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian production of oil, including gas condensate, will fall to 303 million tonnes this year from 306 million in 1995, the government's Centre for Economic Trends said.</p>
<p>It issued the following forecasts in the government bulletin published on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>					 1996     1995     1996     1995</p>
<p>								pct change yr/yr</p>
<p>oil</p>
<p>    including gas condensate   303	306	 -1	 -3</p>
<p>    without gas condensate     295	298	 -1	 -4</p>
<p>    primary refining of oil    173.6    179.1     -3	 -0.1</p>
<p>    gasoline			 270.6    279.3     -3	 +5</p>
<p>    jet engine fuel		  8.8	8.9     -2	 -0.6</p>
<p>    diesel fuel		     45.7     46.5     -2	 +3</p>
<p>    heating oil (mazut)	   62.2     63.1     -1	 -6</p>
<p>    natural gas		    602	596	 +1	 -2</p>
<p>NOTE - figures in millions of tonnes, except for gas, which is in billions of cubic meters</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
